   423	// P1T-FIX8 (sweep (l)): the message a RuntimeError raised by synchronize() already holds (its args[0]), when it is a
   424	// compact ASCII str (every tc_signal message is ASCII): PyException_GetArgs takes a reference to the existing tuple and
   425	// PyUnicode_DATA is the str's own buffer, so nothing is allocated (pybind11's error_already_set::what() formats lazily,
   426	// allocating inside a noexcept function: a bad_alloc there would std::terminate). nullptr when unavailable. The
   427	// pointer is valid while the exception object is alive.
