tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:461:# ======================================================================== lead send-back L2: stopping the watchdog
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:462:# DeviceWaitWatchdog::stop() (dlpack_operand.cpp) must be safe whatever its lock or its join does:
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:463:#  (a) a failed pthread_join must not detach a thread still inside run() (it uses mu_, cv_ and the caller's schedule,
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:465:#  (b) a failed stop-lock must not cost a silent wait until the watchdog's next diagnostic (its notify can then be
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:466:#      missed: the watchdog between its predicate check and its wait).
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:467:# An LD_PRELOAD interposer (pthread_create / mutex lock and unlock / cond clockwait and broadcast / join / detach)
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:468:# recognizes the watchdog thread (the first thread the main thread creates once armed, right before the exit runner;
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:469:# cross-checked by exit_device_wait_watchdogs == 1) and, inside the window from its creation to its join or detach:
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:470:#   * 'lock' n: fails the next n main-thread pthread_mutex_lock calls made from _tc_signal*.so (stop()'s lock), and
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:472:#     arrives before the watchdog waits). The wait from stop()'s first lock attempt to the join's return is measured.
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:473:#   * 'join' n: fails the next n pthread_join calls for the watchdog thread (std::thread::join throws), and holds the
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:474:#     watchdog 50 ms after the wakeup stop() sends (a preempted watchdog). Every mutex / condition-variable call the
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:475:#     watchdog thread makes from _tc_signal*.so is timed; none may come after the detach, and the last one must come
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:477:#   * 'control': nothing fails; the watchdog is joined normally.
tc_signal/tests/test_fix8_findings.py:480:# (5 s), so a missed notify would leave the watchdog asleep for ~4.6 s more. Mutant (h) = stop() reverted to FIX8's.
