   402	  discipline (an error must survive the failure of its own reporting; https://www.sqlite.org/testing.html, as the
   403	  round-8 review cited) - taken: the principle and the fault injection; C++17 `std::bad_alloc` (what the fallback
   404	  catches; its `what()` is a static string); `cudaGetErrorName` returning a runtime-owned `const char*` the caller
   405	  never frees (`.../cuda126_runtime_api_error.txt`); CPython 3.12 atexit (an exception escaping a callback is printed,
   406	  the rest still run). Ours: the plain-data summary of the tagged records, the acknowledged exit report (a report a
   407	  hook raised is consumed only once the hook says it wrote it), and the runner as the last reader in every case.
